<title>EGYPT: Egypt cuts most Feb crude prices against Brent.</title>
<headline>Egypt cuts most Feb crude prices against Brent.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt cut the February price of its Gulf of Suez Blend by 25 cents a barrel against dated Brent, to Brent -$2.35 from -$2.10, the state's Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It raised the price of Ras Gharib crude by five cents against Brent but cut the prices of all other Egyptian crude grades by either 15 or 25 cents, it said.</p>
<p>Following are details of EGPC's February crude prices, all against dated Brent (January differentials in brackets):</p>
<p>    Gulf of Suez    -$2.35  (-$2.10)</p>
<p>    Belayim	   -$3.60  (-$3.35)</p>
<p>    Ras Gharib	-$4.15  (-$4.20)</p>
<p>    Ras Badran	-$3.80  (-$3.65)</p>
<p>    Ras el Behar    -$1.75  (-$1.60)</p>
<p>    Zeit Bay	  -$1.80  (-$1.65)</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
